The condition $x>7y$ is equivalent to $y<x/7$. The line $y=x/7$ runs from the origin to $(2009,287)$ on the right edge, since $2009/7=287<2010$. The region below it is a right triangle with base 2009 and height 287; excluding the line does not affect its area.

For a uniform point, the probability is the favorable area divided by the rectangle's area: $\frac{2009\cdot287/2}{2009\cdot2010}=\frac{287}{4020}$.
Final answer: \frac{287}{4020}
